+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report for taffy
+
+Tests were added with `hegeltest` 0.28.2 (library crate name `hegel`), added via
+`cargo add --dev hegeltest --ignore-rust-version` (taffy pins `rust-version = 1.71`,
+hegeltest requires 1.86 — the dev-dependency MSRV bump is a maintainer decision if
+these tests are upstreamed).
+
+## Properties tested
+
+All property tests are named `hegel_*` and live alongside the existing tests for the
+same functionality. Shared generators (`styles`, `tree_specs`, `available_spaces`,
+`dimensions`, ...) live at the bottom of `tests/hand_written/relayout.rs` and follow
+the skill's "generate configurations, not just payloads" pattern: an arbitrary-but-valid
+`Style` generator (encoding CSS validity rules as construction logic: non-negative
+padding/border/gap/flex-grow/flex-shrink, positive aspect-ratio, margins/insets may be
+negative) and a recursive tree generator on top of it.
+
+1. **Relayout determinism** — `hegel_relayout_is_stable`
+   (`tests/hand_written/relayout.rs`). Computing layout twice in a row with the same
+   available space yields bitwise-identical layouts for every node.
+   *Evidence:* the existing `relayout` unit test in the same file asserts exactly this
+   for one hand-built tree.
+
+2. **Cache invalidation is layout-neutral** — `hegel_relayout_after_mark_dirty_is_stable`
+   (`tests/hand_written/relayout.rs`). Marking an arbitrary node dirty and recomputing
+   (with nothing changed) reproduces the identical layout.
+   *Evidence:* `mark_dirty` docs ("Marks the layout of this node and its ancestors as
+   outdated") + the caching tests; caches are supposed to be a pure optimisation.
+
+3. **Finite outputs for finite inputs** — `hegel_layout_outputs_are_finite`
+   (`tests/hand_written/relayout.rs`). For finite style values and finite/intrinsic
+   available space, every f32 in every node's `Layout` is finite (no NaN/infinity).
+   *Evidence:* `Layout` is consumed by renderers; all style inputs generated are finite
+   and bounded, so any non-finite output would be an arithmetic bug.
+
+4. **`Display::None` hides the whole subtree** — `hegel_display_none_root_zeroes_entire_subtree`
+   (`tests/hand_written/relayout.rs`). With an arbitrary subtree under a `Display::None`
+   root, every node's size and location are zero.
+   *Evidence:* `toggle_root_display_none_with_children` unit test; `compute_hidden_layout`
+   ("Each hidden node has zero size and is placed at the origin").
+
+5. **Incremental relayout ≡ from-scratch layout** — `hegel_incremental_relayout_matches_fresh_tree`
+   (`tests/hand_written/relayout.rs`). Build a tree, lay it out, apply one random
+   mutation (`set_style`, `remove`, `add_child` of a new leaf, or
+   `remove_child_at_index`), recompute, and compare bitwise against a freshly built
+   tree with the same final structure laid out once.
+   *Evidence:* every mutating method is expected to invalidate affected caches (all of
+   them call `mark_dirty` — see below for the one that doesn't); the `relayout` and
+   caching tests encode the same expectation for specific cases. **FAILS — see
+   Suspected bugs #1.**
+
+6. **Rounded layouts are whole pixels** — `hegel_rounded_layout_values_are_whole_numbers`
+   (`tests/hand_written/rounding.rs`). With rounding enabled (the default), location,
+   size, content_size, scrollbar_size, border and padding in every node's layout are
+   whole numbers. (`Layout::margin` is exempt: `round_layout` does not touch it.)
+   *Evidence:* `round_layout` doc comment ("Rounds the calculated layout to exact pixel
+   values") and its implementation.
+
+7. **Rounding leaves no gaps** — `hegel_rounding_leaves_no_gaps_between_adjacent_children`
+   (`tests/hand_written/rounding.rs`). In a single-line flex row with fractional child
+   sizes, fractional container size/padding, and non-spacing justification, each child's
+   rounded right edge equals the next child's rounded left edge exactly.
+   *Evidence:* the existing `rounding_doesnt_leave_gaps` unit test and the `round_layout`
+   doc comment ("In order to ensure that no gaps in the layout are introduced ...").
+
+8. **Min/max clamping semantics** — `hegel_leaf_size_is_clamped_by_min_and_max`
+   (`tests/hand_written/min_max_overrides.rs`). For a leaf with definite size/min/max
+   lengths (rounding disabled), the computed size is exactly
+   `max(min(size, max_size), min_size)` per axis — min wins over max.
+   *Evidence:* the `min_overrides_max`, `max_overrides_size`, `min_overrides_size` unit
+   tests in the same file.
+
+9. **Parse robustness** — `hegel_style_from_str_never_panics`
+   (`tests/hand_written/parse.rs`, new file — no parse test file existed). The `parse`
+   feature's `FromStr` impls (`Dimension`, `LengthPercentage`, `LengthPercentageAuto`,
+   `AvailableSpace`, `AlignItems`, `AlignContent`, `GridAutoFlow`,
+   `Min`/`Max`/`TrackSizingFunction`, `RepetitionCount`, `GridPlacement`,
+   `GridTemplateComponent`) return `Err` and never panic, on arbitrary Unicode text,
+   number/unit-shaped strings, and almost-valid CSS.
+   *Evidence:* `FromStr::Err = ParseError` signatures; feature docs "Implement `FromStr`
+   trait for Taffy style types".
+
+10. **Stateful model test of tree mutation** — `hegel_tree_mutations_match_model`
+    (`src/tree/taffy_tree.rs`, inside the existing unit-test module, using
+    `#[hegel::state_machine]`). Rules `new_leaf`, `add_child`, `insert_child_at_index`,
+    `remove_child_at_index`, `replace_child_at_index`, `remove`, `set_children`, and a
+    `child_at_index` query run against both `TaffyTree` and a HashMap-based
+    parent/children reference model; an invariant asserts `children()`, `parent()` and
+    `total_node_count()` agree with the model after every step.
+    *Evidence:* the documented per-method semantics (including `set_children`'s
+    documented detach-from-previous-parent behaviour, cross-checked by the
+    `set_children_reparents` unit test) and the existing `add_child`/
+    `insert_child_at_index`/`remove_child_at_index` unit tests.
+
+## Test results
+
